ONLINE ACTIVITY #3
GitHub Fork, Update, and Pull Request

Practice using GitHub to fork an existing repository, modify files, commit changes, and submit a Pull Request.

Instructions:

1. Fork the repository the instructor will provide
2. Create a new file named {studentnumber}.html (profile page).
3. Add the required information/content to your student file.
4. Link your GitHub pages to your name, so users can click your name and be taken to your GitHub Pages
5. In your forked repository, update the existing index page to link your profile page.
6. Commit both changes to your forked repository.
7. Create a Pull Request (PR) from your fork to the original repository.

Submission
In a pdf file, include the screenshot of the following:
1. YOUR forked repo showing the new files you created
2. page showing the commits in YOUR forked repository
3. page showing you did a pull request to the main repo


